<title>TURKEY: Turkey's cotton exports since Sept at 37,208 T.</title>
<headline>Turkey's cotton exports since Sept at 37,208 T.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's cotton exports since the export season began in September 1996 reached 37,208 tonnes until January 10 and earned it $52.8 million, Aegean Exporters Union officials said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>They said no comparison was available for the same period in the previous 1995/96 harvest year but said Turkey exported a total of 58,465 tonnes in the 1995/96 export season (Sept-Aug), when its exports were limited to a quota of 100,000 tonnes. The government later abolished the quota.</p>
<p>Turkey last month revised its cotton output for 1996/97 (Oct-July) to 792,414 tonnes from 783,735 tonnes, down from a record output in 1995/96 of 851,487 tonnes.</p>
<p>Textile producers and ginners said earlier that they expected 200,000 tonnes of imports in early 1997 to make up for a shortfall in output.</p>
<p>--Ercan Ersoy, Ankara Newsroom, 90-312-4462940</p>
</text>
